BIT READ / WRITE — THE FOUR CORE OPERATIONS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

// Check if i-th bit is set  (0-indexed from right)
bool isSet = (x >> i) & 1;

// Set the i-th bit  (force it to 1)
x = x | (1 << i);

// Clear the i-th bit  (force it to 0)
x = x & ~(1 << i);

// Toggle the i-th bit  (flip it)
x = x ^ (1 << i);
Example with x = 0b1010 (10), i = 1:
  Check:   (10 >> 1) & 1  =  5 & 1  =  1    ✓ bit 1 is set
  Clear:   10 & ~(1<<1)   =  10 & ~2 =  8    result: 0b1000
  Toggle:  10 ^ (1<<1)    =  10 ^ 2  =  8    result: 0b1000
