LOWEST SET BIT TRICKS
━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━━

// Isolate the lowest set bit
int lowest = x & (-x);

Why it works:
  -x in two's complement flips all bits then adds 1.
  12  =  ...001100
 -12  =  ...110100
 12 & -12  =  000100  →  isolates the rightmost 1.

// Clear the lowest set bit
x = x & (x - 1);

Why it works:
  x - 1 flips the lowest set bit and all bits below it.
  12  =  1100
  11  =  1011
  12 & 11  =  1000  →  lowest set bit is gone.

// Used in: counting set bits manually, Fenwick Tree (BIT)
